{number: 30}
{title: Hark! The Herald Angels Sing}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] Hark! The herald [D] angels [G] sing,
"Glory to the [C] new-born [D] King!
[G] Peace on earth, and [D] mercy [Em] mild,
[A7] God and sinners [D] reconciled!"
[G] Joyful, all ye [C] nations [D] rise,
[G] Join the triumph [C] of the [D] skies;
[C] With the angelic [Am] host pro-[E7] claim,
"[Am] Christ is [D7] born in [G] Bethlehem!"
[C] Hark! the herald [Am] angels [E7] sing,
"[Am] Glory [D7] to the [G] new-born King!"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Christ, by highest [D] heav'n a-[G] dored,
Christ, the ever-[C] lasting [D] Lord,
[G] Late in time be-[D] hold Him [Em] come,
[A7] Offspring of a [D] virgin's womb.
[G] Veiled in flesh the [C] Godhead [D] see,
[G] Hail the incarnate [C] Dei-[D] ty!
[C] Pleased as Man with [Am] man to [E7] dwell;
[Am] Jesus, [D7] our Im-[G] manuel!
[C] Hark! the herald [Am] angels [E7] sing,
"[Am] Glory [D7] to the [G] new-born King!"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Hail, the heav'nly [D] Prince of [G] Peace!
Hail, the Sun of [C] Righteous-[D] ness!
[G] Light and life to [D] all He [Em] brings,
[A7] Ris'n with healing [D] in His wings.
[G] Mild, He leaves His [C] throne on [D] high,
[G] Born that man no [C] more may [D] die;
[C] Born to raise the [Am] sons of [E7] earth;
[Am] Born to [D7] give them [G] second birth,
[C] Hark! the herald [Am] angels [E7] sing,
"[Am] Glory [D7] to the [G] new-born King!"
{end_of_verse}
